566
00:24:17,760 --> 00:24:18,280
Not at all.

567
00:24:18,440 --> 00:24:20,010
Especially psychological safety.

568
00:24:20,350 --> 00:24:28,320
Remotely, you have to be so much more intentional about building trust and connection because there's no shared physical space, no water cooler moments.

569
00:24:28,380 --> 00:24:31,350
So how can language help build that culture right from the start of a call?

570
00:24:31,610 --> 00:24:32,850
Simple techniques work well.

571
00:24:32,990 --> 00:24:36,140
The sources suggest start meetings with two-word moods.

572
00:24:36,260 --> 00:24:40,950
Two word moods like like tired, focused or excited, caffeinated.

573
00:24:41,290 --> 00:24:42,710
Just a quick human check in.

574
00:24:42,790 --> 00:24:47,320
It sparks light conversation, helps people gauge the room's energy before diving into business.

575
00:24:47,480 --> 00:24:48,020
I like that.

576
00:24:48,790 --> 00:24:49,900
Humanizes the screen.

577
00:24:50,280 --> 00:24:51,740
What about inclusive language?

578
00:24:52,120 --> 00:24:53,720
Absolutely vital for belonging.

579
00:24:54,360 --> 00:24:55,870
Simple shifts make a difference.

580
00:24:56,180 --> 00:24:58,410
Use inclusive language like team instead of guys.

581
00:24:58,870 --> 00:25:01,930
Seems small, but signals respect globally.

582
00:25:02,330 --> 00:25:05,840
And also explicitly acknowledging cultural holidays openly.

583
00:25:06,300 --> 00:25:10,250
Recognizing and respecting time off or celebrations for colleagues around the world.

584
00:25:10,410 --> 00:25:13,030
Builds that sense of a truly global, respectful team.

585
00:25:13,160 --> 00:25:14,000
Okay, feedback.

586
00:25:14,260 --> 00:25:17,870
We touched on conflict, but what about general constructive feedback remotely?

587
00:25:18,210 --> 00:25:20,310
Finesse is required, the golden rule.

588
00:25:20,770 --> 00:25:24,840
Provide candid feedback privately first, praising publicly later.

589
00:25:25,500 --> 00:25:28,400
Build people up in public, correct in private.

590
00:25:28,420 --> 00:25:28,900
Makes sense.

591
00:25:29,510 --> 00:25:32,950
But how do you deliver that private feedback without triggering defensiveness?

592
00:25:33,770 --> 00:25:35,350
